lotr.waypoint.ACROST=Acrost
lotr.waypoint.ACROST.info=Fishing village of Anfalas. It suffers from tides more often than other settlements of Anfalas.
lotr.waypoint.AGRUN_HAZR.info=The old fortress of Rhudaur. In time of Angmar rise, was guardian of Arthedain borders. Nowadays, mountain orcs occupied it.
lotr.waypoint.AGRUN_HAZR=Agrun Hazr
lotr.waypoint.AIN_AL_HARAD=Ain-al-Harad
lotr.waypoint.AIN_AL_HARAD.info=The Eye of Harad, the legendary southern city, was considered a miracle even among the haradrim themselves.
lotr.waypoint.ALDBURG=Aldburg
lotr.waypoint.ALDBURG.info=The first capital of Rohan, Aldburg is the oldest city in Riddermark, ruled by the third Marshal of Rohan.
lotr.waypoint.AMON_ANGREN=Amon Angren
lotr.waypoint.AMON_ANGREN.info=The dark hill in Mordor, on which the Nazgûl fortress stands.
lotr.waypoint.AMON_DIN=Amon Din
lotr.waypoint.AMON_DIN.info=The Hill of Silence is the closest signal hill to Minas Tirith. It is a rocky, barren hill with empty slopes. Birds and animals are rarely found on Amon Din, and people use it exclusively as an outpost. Guards on Amon Din watch the crossing of the Anduin near Cair Andros and the passage to Ithilien from Dagorlad.
lotr.waypoint.AMON_EITEL=Amon Eithel
lotr.waypoint.AMON_EITEL.info=The largest city of Harondor, built by the men of Gondor. Due to the threat of Harnedor's invasion, it was completely abandoned. However, the rangers of Ithilien are still hiding in the high walls of this city to fight the southerners.
lotr.waypoint.AMON_EREB=Amon Ereb
lotr.waypoint.AMON_EREB.info=A wide, gently sloping hill between Ramdal and the river Gelion, which overlooked the southern plains of Eastern Beleriand. It was of great strategic importance because it was an excellent viewpoint.
lotr.waypoint.AMON_HEN=Amon Hen
lotr.waypoint.AMON_HEN.info=The Hill of Vision, an ancient outpost of the Gondor.
lotr.waypoint.AMON_LHAW=Amon Lhaw
lotr.waypoint.AMON_LHAW.info=The Hill of Hearing, an ancient outpost of the Gondor.
lotr.waypoint.ANDUIN_CROSSROADS.info=The fork between the Anduin Road and the Dol Guldur road.
lotr.waypoint.ANDUIN_CROSSROADS=Tharanadun
lotr.waypoint.ANDUIN_MOUTH=Ethir Anduin
lotr.waypoint.ANDUIN_MOUTH.info=The place where the Anduin flows into the ocean, branching into many streams.
lotr.waypoint.ANGSUL=Angsul
lotr.waypoint.ANGSUL.info=The last fortress in front of the majestic Carn-dûm. Angsul was the second residence of the Witch-king. Now, like Karn Doom, it has been destroyed.
lotr.waypoint.ANNODRUN=Annodrun
lotr.waypoint.ANNODRUN.info=Крепость Аннодран является самой западной твердней королевства Гондора. Крепость обороняет бухту и устье реки Лефнал, которая ведет к единственному поселению на дальнем западе Гондора
lotr.waypoint.ANNOGWAIN=Annogwain
lotr.waypoint.ANNOGWAIN.info=The only major settlement in the far west of Gondor. The settlement is protected by the fortress of Annodrun downstream of Lefnal. Residents sometimes visit the Bridge in order to exchange wood for the necessary materials: metals, fish
lotr.waypoint.ANNUMINAS=Annuminas
lotr.waypoint.ANNUMINAS.info=The city, once the capital of the kingdom of Arnor, is located on the southeastern shore of Lake Evendim (Nenuial). It contained one of the palantirs. The city was built by King Elendil and was his main residence. Later, Fornost Erain became the capital.
lotr.waypoint.ATHRAD_GILRAIN=Athrad Gilrain
lotr.waypoint.ATHRAD_GILRAIN.info=Gilrain's Ford, through which the Lebeninians move to the mountain mines.
lotr.waypoint.ARCHET=Archet
lotr.waypoint.ARCHET.info=The town of the Bree people on the edge of the Chetwood; trades in deforestation.
lotr.waypoint.ARGONATH=Argonath
lotr.waypoint.ARGONATH.info=Pillars of Kings: Two huge statues of Isildur and Anarion by the banks of the river Anduin, guarding the old northern borders of Gondor.
lotr.waypoint.ARGOND=Argond
lotr.waypoint.ARGOND.info=The "High Rock" from ыindarin, was a fortress built at the end of Cardolan's existence. The building was considered the most beautiful fortress in the whole kingdom until it fell into disrepair.
lotr.waypoint.ARNACH.info=Lossarnach's capital city, located in the center of the province. Large orchards flourished here, providing much of the necessary fruit and medicinal herbs for Minas Tirith.
lotr.waypoint.ARNACH=Arnach
lotr.waypoint.ARVEDUI_MINES=Arvedui mines
lotr.waypoint.ARVEDUI_MINES.info=Abandoned mines in the Blue Mountains. The last king of Artedain and his people settled here, fleeing from the Angmar army after the fall of the kingdom. These mines are now empty.
lotr.waypoint.ASH_KARAZH=Ash-Karazh
lotr.waypoint.ASH_KARAZH.info=War city of Khand. Here armies training, checking and go to war.
lotr.waypoint.ATHILIN=Athilin
lotr.waypoint.ATHILIN.info=The fortress was built on fairly advanced positions, which allowed it to occupy a key position in the defense of Angmar. The Black Numenorians bravely defended the fortress during the Angmar Wars. But they were defeated. The fortress is currently under restoration.
lotr.waypoint.BALCARAS=Balcaras
lotr.waypoint.BALCARAS.info=A city of Wagon People and one of the few villages of this nomadic people.
lotr.waypoint.BARACK_TULUN=Barak-Thulun
lotr.waypoint.BARACK_TULUN.info=The great capital of the mighty Khand, in which the Khan sits on his throne, cast from gold in the shape of a dragon's mouth.
lotr.waypoint.BARAD_DUR=Barad-dûr
lotr.waypoint.BARAD_DUR.info=The Dark Tower: the fortress of Sauron, Lord of Mordor, as well as the place of imprisonment and torture of all his enemies. The height of the main tower of Barad-dûr was more than 200 meters. Barad-dûr is the capital of Mordor, where Sauron himself is constantly located and from there he manages his possessions. The governor of Barad-dûr is the Mouth of Sauron.
lotr.waypoint.BARAD_HARN=Barad Harn
lotr.waypoint.BARAD_HARN.info=The city is named after the tall numenorian lighthouse located in its center. The long wars and invasions of the Harnedrim almost destroyed the settlement itself, but the lighthouse remained untouched. At the moment, it is the hideout of the rangers of Ithilien.
lotr.waypoint.BARAZ_DUM=Baraz-dûm
lotr.waypoint.BARAZ_DUM.info=Great city of Stiffbeards dwarves.
lotr.waypoint.BARAZ_ZIGIL=Baraz-Zigil
lotr.waypoint.BARAZ_ZIGIL.info=The southern peak of the Orocarni mountain range. The sacred mountain of the Blacklocks and Stonefoots.
lotr.waypoint.BARKA=Barka
lotr.waypoint.BARKA.info=A village whose main industry is agriculture. Travelers from Ered Luin often pass through it.
lotr.waypoint.BAZYLAN=Bazylan
lotr.waypoint.BAZYLAN.info=The city of Easterlings, which is said to have been founded by a powerful nobleman and named after his beloved cat.
lotr.waypoint.BEAR_ISLAND=Bear island
lotr.waypoint.BEAR_ISLAND.info=A small island of the ice bay of Forochel, surrounded by ice. It is home to families of polar bears, whose fur is especially appreciated by Lossoth.
lotr.waypoint.BELEGOST=Belegost
lotr.waypoint.BELEGOST.info=The ancient city of the dwarves of the Blue Mountains, built in Ancient Days. It was destroyed after the War of Wrath, but then rebuilt by the dwarves.
lotr.waypoint.BEORN=Beorn house.
lotr.waypoint.BEORN.info=The former home of the skinchanger Beorn, now grown to the size of a small town.
lotr.waypoint.BIZAR_ATRAD=Bizar-atrâd
lotr.waypoint.BIZAR_ATRAD.info=A long-abandoned watchtower of the Grey Mountains dwarves. Legend has it that ancestral spirits can be seen at its summit.
lotr.waypoint.BLACK_COAST=Durfalas
lotr.waypoint.BLACK_COAST.info=The rocky eastern shores of Pertorogwaith.
lotr.waypoint.BLOOD_RIVER.info=The Bloodflow, a black and choking stream which runs through the land of the Half-trolls.
lotr.waypoint.BLOOD_RIVER=Sereghir
lotr.waypoint.BORDER_TOWN.info=A city near the easterling border, living off trade with Dorwinion.
lotr.waypoint.BORDER_TOWN=Tharagal
lotr.waypoint.BRANDYWINE_BRIDGE=Brandywine bridge
lotr.waypoint.BRANDYWINE_BRIDGE.info=A bridge spanning the Brandywine river, as well as the Shire border.
lotr.waypoint.BREE=Bree
lotr.waypoint.BREE.info=The main city of the lands of Bree, known for its cheerful inhabitants - humans and hobbits.
lotr.waypoint.BROCKENBORINGS=Brockenborings
lotr.waypoint.BROCKENBORINGS.info=A village on rocky hills, surrounded by Badger holes. The village is adjacent to Scary.
lotr.waypoint.BUCKLEBURY=Bucklebury
lotr.waypoint.BUCKLEBURY.info=The main village of Buckland, the home of the Owner of the Brandinorye.
lotr.waypoint.BYWATER=Bywater
lotr.waypoint.BYWATER.info=The village is located on the Eastern Road along the Bywater Pool, where the famous Green Dragon tavern is located.
lotr.waypoint.CAIR_ANDROS=Cair Andros
lotr.waypoint.CAIR_ANDROS.info=A fortified island in Anduin, named "Foam Ship". The fortress of Cairo Andros was used to protect Calenardhon (later Rohan) from the attack of the easterlings of Rhûn.
lotr.waypoint.CALEMBEL=Calembel
lotr.waypoint.CALEMBEL.info=A large city, the largest city of Lamedon, located at the fords of the Ciril River.
lotr.waypoint.CALENHAD=Calenhad
lotr.waypoint.CALENHAD.info=The sixth signal hill of Gondor, which was lit only when absolutely necessary, such as during the War of the Ring. Calenhad Hill was relatively low, with a green turf area at the top.
lotr.waypoint.CAPE_OF_FOROCHEL=Cape of Forochel
lotr.waypoint.CAPE_OF_FOROCHEL.info=A snow-covered cape overlooking the dangerous waters of the Icy Bay.
lotr.waypoint.CARACH_ANGREN=Crach Angren
lotr.waypoint.CARACH_ANGREN.info="Iron Jaws" is a protected mountain pass between Udûn and Gorgoroth.
lotr.waypoint.CARAS_CELAIRNEN=Caras Celairnen
lotr.waypoint.CARAS_CELAIRNEN.info=Arthedain's western outpost on the River Lhun. Ruined, but the Lhun people tell legends of a beautiful white tower once standing here, and graceful ships with triangular sails sailing the river.
lotr.waypoint.CARAS_GALADHON=Caras Caladhon
lotr.waypoint.CARAS_GALADHON.info=City of Galadhrim in Lothlorien, as well as the capital of the entire Golden Forest.
lotr.waypoint.CARN_DUM=Carn Dûm
lotr.waypoint.CARN_DUM.info=A fortress on the northern foothills of the Misty Mountains, the capital of Angmar.
lotr.waypoint.CARROCK=Carrock
lotr.waypoint.CARROCK.info=A rocky islet on the upper approaches to the Anduin River, north of the Old Ford. According to legend, every night a mighty bear climbs this rock to look at the moon.
lotr.waypoint.CEDAR_ROAD=Cedar_road
lotr.waypoint.CEDAR_ROAD.info=Durable cedar wood is highly valued in the south. When Sauron returned to Mordor, he demanded cedar wood as tribute.
lotr.waypoint.CERIN_AMROTH=Cerin Amroth
lotr.waypoint.CERIN_AMROTH.info=The great green hill in the middle of Lothlorien, from where, as they say, you can see the southern Mirkwood.
lotr.waypoint.CIRITH_UNGOL=Cirith Ungol
lotr.waypoint.CIRITH_UNGOL.info=A dark twisted "Spider Pass" in the mountains of Mordor, guarded by an Ork outpost.
lotr.waypoint.COAST_CITY.info=One of the small towns of the southern coasts, which nevertheless commands many ferocious swords and a terrible devotion to the great eye of the North.
lotr.waypoint.COAST_CITY=Nuremin
lotr.waypoint.COAST_FORTRESS=Ghat Azrazain
lotr.waypoint.COAST_FORTRESS.info=The ancient Numenor fortress, built to watch the surrounding fields. It fell into the hands of the Haradrim a long time ago.
lotr.waypoint.COAST_RIVER_TOWN.info=A city on the southern coast of the Astrasir River, which controls many merchant ships passing between the cedar forests and the great cities of the South.
lotr.waypoint.COAST_RIVER_TOWN=Tavinen
lotr.waypoint.COMBE=Combe
lotr.waypoint.COMBE.info=A village of people on the road to Chetwood.
lotr.waypoint.CORGONIN=Corgonin
lotr.waypoint.CORGONIN.info=A small settlement of Anfalasa near Calenhir River. The main occupation of the locals is agriculture and animal husbandry. There is also fishing
lotr.waypoint.CORSAIRS_LANDING=Corsairs landing
lotr.waypoint.CORSAIRS_LANDING.info=In the time of Helm Hammerhand, the fleet of Umbar landed here and fought alongside the dunlendings to defeat the people of Rohan.
lotr.waypoint.CROSSINGS_ERUI=Crossings of Erui
lotr.waypoint.CROSSINGS_ERUI.info=The fords of the river Erui in Lossarnach. Many Gondorians died here during the Kin-strife.
lotr.waypoint.CROSSINGS_OF_HARAD=Crossing of Harad
lotr.waypoint.CROSSINGS_OF_HARAD.info=This river represents the border of the lands of Harondor. From here, the road runs south to the Sunny lands of Haradwaith.
lotr.waypoint.CROSSINGS_OF_LITHNEN=Crossings of Lithnen
lotr.waypoint.CROSSINGS_OF_LITHNEN.info=Fords across Litnen River, leading further into the eastern lands. Often in past centuries, these waters were stained the color of blood by the warriors of Gondor.
lotr.waypoint.CROSSINGS_OF_POROS=Crossing of Poros
lotr.waypoint.CROSSINGS_OF_POROS.info=The way to Harondor is across the Poros River. Nearby stands a large mound, where the twin sons of King Folcwine of Rohan are buried.
lotr.waypoint.CROSSROADS_ITHILIEN=Crossroads of Ithilien
lotr.waypoint.CROSSROADS_ITHILIEN.info=There was once a majestic statue of the king at this abandoned intersection. This statue may be destroyed now, but its head is still crowned with a crown of gold and silver.
lotr.waypoint.custom.andMore=and %d more
lotr.waypoint.custom.info=It is a waypoint for the fellowship "%d"
lotr.waypoint.custom=%s (My own)
lotr.waypoint.DAINS_HALLS=Dains halls
lotr.waypoint.DAINS_HALLS.info=The colony of Durin's Folk in the Grey Mountains, abandoned after Dain's death in battle with the ice dragon.
lotr.waypoint.NORDINBAD=Nordinbad
lotr.waypoint.NORDINBAD.info=Norndinband was a former great dwarven fortress in the Grey Mountains. After the dwarves fled, it was occupied by orcs and ogres. Now, the fire-breathing dragon Urgost lives there.
lotr.waypoint.DALE_CITY=Dale
lotr.waypoint.DALE_CITY.info=The prosperous city of Dale kingdom at the foot of the Lonely Mountain. It was destroyed by Smaug the Terrible, but rebuilt under the leadership of King Bard after the death of the dragon.
lotr.waypoint.DALE_CROSSROADS=Bahorbad
lotr.waypoint.DALE_CROSSROADS.info=A huge trading city at the intersection of the six highways of Dale. These lands are a place of concentration of itinerant merchants and dalish markets.
lotr.waypoint.DALE_PORT=Harbold
lotr.waypoint.DALE_PORT.info=The southern port of Dale kingdom and an extremely important point on Dorwinion trade routes.
lotr.waypoint.DEEPHALLOW=Deephallow
lotr.waypoint.DEEPHALLOW.info=A village on the banks of the Brandywine River.
lotr.waypoint.DERNDINGLE=Derngingle
lotr.waypoint.DERNDINGLE.info=The meeting place of the ents of Fangorn, located in a hidden clearing.
lotr.waypoint.DESERT_RIVER_TOWN=Ayukaf-Amam
lotr.waypoint.DESERT_RIVER_TOWN.info=A city of nomads who control the river near the Gulf of Harad.
lotr.waypoint.DESERT_TOWN.info=A camp of southern nomads, where hermits from many tribes go to trade and tell tales in the shadow of Emin Litnen.
lotr.waypoint.DESERT_TOWN=Izdi-Ilel
lotr.waypoint.DIMRILL_DALE=Dimrill dale
lotr.waypoint.DIMRILL_DALE.info=Azanulbizar, Nanduhirion, "Valley of the Misty streams" - the valley lying near the eastern gate of Kazad-Dûm. Durin the Deathless ended his wanderings here, having seen a crown of stars above his head at night in the reflection of lake Kheled-zâram. After that, he decided to establish his kingdom here.
lotr.waypoint.DOL_AMROTH=Dol Amroth
lotr.waypoint.DOL_AMROTH.info=A mighty castle and city on the shores of Belfalas, ruled by the Prince of Dol Amroth, a vassal of Gondor. The fortress was named in memory of Amroth, King of Lorien. Dol Amroth was inhabited by the descendants of the Numenorians, dark-haired and gray-eyed. Even during the days of the War of the Ring, many of the inhabitants of Dol Amroth had pure Numenorian blood, and there were people among them who not only knew Sindarin, but also used it as a language of everyday communication.
lotr.waypoint.DOL_BARAN=Dol Baran
lotr.waypoint.DOL_BARAN.info=Dol Baran is the southernmost peak of the Misty Mountains. A round, flower-crowned hill with a green base. It is the gathering place of Dunlending raiders who invade the Gap of Rohan.
lotr.waypoint.DOL_GULDUR=Dol Guldur
lotr.waypoint.DOL_GULDUR.info=The Mountain of Sorcery was the fortress-lair of the Necromancer before he fled south to Mordor. Now this fortress was occupied by the Enemy's servant, Nazgûl Khamûl.
lotr.waypoint.DOL_NINDEN=Dol Ninden
lotr.waypoint.DOL_NINDEN.info=A hill located in the heart of Minhiriath. There is an old watchtower at the top, and there is a dense oak forest around the hill.
lotr.waypoint.DORWINION_COURT=Gwynne Daer
lotr.waypoint.DORWINION_COURT.info=The capital, center of trade, science, and culture of the elven-human kingdom of Dorwinion.
lotr.waypoint.DORWINION_CROSSROADS.info=The city of Thoris, a descendant of King Bladorthin. There is a trade route from Dorwinion to Dale.
lotr.waypoint.DORWINION_CROSSROADS=Thorisborg
lotr.waypoint.DORWINION_FORD=Gwynost
lotr.waypoint.DORWINION_FORD.info=A fortress guarding the passage to the lands of the Rhûn from Dorwinion.
lotr.waypoint.DORWINION_HILLS=Amon Gwynne
lotr.waypoint.DORWINION_HILLS.info=The highest peak in the hills of Dorwinion.
lotr.waypoint.DORWINION_PORT=Gwynlond
lotr.waypoint.DORWINION_PORT.info=The wine harbors of Kelduin, through which the elves-Avari of Dorwinion send goods to their relatives in the Woodland Realm.
lotr.waypoint.DRUWAITH_YAUR.info=A mysterious forest inhabited by many mystical creatures that are considered long-forgotten...
lotr.waypoint.DRUWAITH_YAUR=rú-Weith-Yaur
lotr.waypoint.DUNHARROW=Dunharrow
lotr.waypoint.DUNHARROW.info=The Rohirrim hideout is under Dwimorberg, the ghost mountain. They say that a living person cannot walk the path of the dead.
lotr.waypoint.DURTHANG=Durthang
lotr.waypoint.DURTHANG.info=A mighty orcish fortress built on the slopes of the Ephel Dúath.
lotr.waypoint.DUWARDAIN=Duwardain
lotr.waypoint.DUWARDAIN.info=A large settlement of the Lhun people, located next to the ruined tower of Arnor. It is rumored that the evil spirits of the tower come out at night to hunt the people of these lands. Despite this, warriors from all over the Lhun valley flock there.
lotr.waypoint.DWARROWVALE=Dwarrowvale
lotr.waypoint.DWARROWVALE.info=An old village that Thrór, Thráin, and Thorin are said to have visited during their long wanderings through Eriador.
lotr.waypoint.DWIMORBERG=Dwimorberg
lotr.waypoint.DWIMORBERG.info=A large mountain with black, gloomy slopes, where the Paths of the Dead began. Also called the "Mountain of Ghosts."
lotr.waypoint.EAGLES_EYRIE=Eagles eyrie
lotr.waypoint.EAGLES_EYRIE.info=The great ledge of rock on the eastern side of the Misty Mountains, accessible only by air. Manwe eagles live here.
lotr.waypoint.EAST_BIGHT.info=It was once the first settlement of the woodmen. Once there was a part of the Green Forest, until the ambitions of people turned the forest into a monotonous plain. Easterlings took advantage of this, completely destroying the city.
lotr.waypoint.EAST_BIGHT=Old forestland
lotr.waypoint.EASTERN_GUARD=Eastern guard
lotr.waypoint.EASTERN_GUARD.info=A fortress, guarding the road on the border of Mordor and Rhûn.
lotr.waypoint.EAST_FOROCHEL=East Forochel
lotr.waypoint.EAST_FOROCHEL.info=East of Forochel Bay, where some people of the Lossoth people live
lotr.waypoint.EASTMARK=Eastmark
lotr.waypoint.EASTMARK.info=The eastern part of Rohan. It is bordered on the north by Wold, on the west by Vestemnet, on the east by Anduin, and on the south by Eastfold.
lotr.waypoint.EAST_PEAK=Barak-Shathur
lotr.waypoint.EAST_PEAK.info="Cloud Axe" is the eastern peak of the Iron Hills. Beneath it lies the Dwarven settlement of Barak Kizdin, or "Axe Hall."
lotr.waypoint.EAST_RHOVANION_ROAD=East Rhovanion road
lotr.waypoint.EAST_RHOVANION_ROAD.info=An old crossroads on the border of the Anduin Valley, Brown and Wild Lands.
lotr.waypoint.EDHELLOND=Edhellond
lotr.waypoint.EDHELLOND.info=The ancient haven of Sindar in the south of Gondor. Initially, the haven was tiny and founded by a few fishing people. Later, the iathrim elves, wishing to find a new home far from the Noldor kingdoms, sailed there on three ships. The people were afraid of the elves and fled to the mountains. The elves used this settlement to build ships bound for Valinor. When the last ship sailed, Gondor occupied this abandoned haven.
lotr.waypoint.EDORAS=Edoras
lotr.waypoint.EDORAS.info=Capital of Rohan, located on a hill in the valley of White Mountains. In the city stands the famous Golden Palaces of Meduseld, where King of the Mark rules.
lotr.waypoint.EILENACH=Eilenach
lotr.waypoint.EILENACH.info=The second signal hill from Minas Tirith, as well as the highest point of the Drúadan Forest.
lotr.waypoint.EMYN_ARNEN=Emyn Arnen
lotr.waypoint.EMYN_ARNEN.info=In the best of times, these hills were the residence of several noble and wealthy gondorian families, including the House of Stewards.
lotr.waypoint.ENCHANTED_RIVER=Enchanted river
lotr.waypoint.ENCHANTED_RIVER.info=Here the elven path crosses a gloomy black river. Travelers should avoid these waters, because anyone who touches them will fall asleep forever...
lotr.waypoint.ENDIL=Endil
lotr.waypoint.ENDIL.info=An important military city on the shores of Belfalas Bay.
lotr.waypoint.ENDRIST=Endrist
lotr.waypoint.ENDRIST.info=The southern fortress of Arthedain rises on a green hill. The inhabitants of Cardolan fled here during the Angmar Wars. However, this refuge did not become their new home, and the fortress was destroyed.
lotr.waypoint.ENEDWAITH_ROAD=Enedwaith road
lotr.waypoint.ENEDWAITH_ROAD.info=Since the fall of the kingdom of Arnor and the weakening of Gondor's power, these sections of the old Royal Highway have been abandoned, and the surrounding outposts have fallen into ruins.
lotr.waypoint.ENTWADE=Entwade
lotr.waypoint.ENTWADE.info=A ford across the river Entwash, bridging the Eastemnet and the Westemnet.
lotr.waypoint.EREBOR=Erebor
lotr.waypoint.EREBOR.info=The Lonely Mountain. Herein lies the Kingdom under the Mountain, a realm of Durin's Folk.
lotr.waypoint.ERECH=Erech
lotr.waypoint.ERECH.info=A great steep hill, believed to be haunted, and known for the mysterious black stone which stands upon the summit.
lotr.waypoint.EREGOST=Eregost
lotr.waypoint.EREGOST.info=The second most important fortress of Belphalas. The gathering place of Prince Dol Amroth's army
lotr.waypoint.ERELAS=Erelas
lotr.waypoint.ERELAS.info=The fourth beacon-hill of Gondor. Bare and treeless, it is easily sighted from the surrounding lands.
lotr.waypoint.ERYN_VORN=Eryn Vorn
lotr.waypoint.ERYN_VORN.info=A dark forest inhabited by mysterious people...
lotr.waypoint.ETHRING=Ethring
lotr.waypoint.ETHRING.info=The city is a crossing over the Ringlo River, located on the road from Pelargir to Erech.
lotr.waypoint.FELAK_GUNUD=Felak-Gunud
lotr.waypoint.FELAK_GUNUD.info=A huge quarry, created by Nagar, the son of Aegnor the Dark, to rebuild Farak-dûm in Nargûn-Khazad. It still works today.
lotr.waypoint.FARANEL=Faranel
lotr.waypoint.FARANEL.info=The northernmost stronghold of Arthedain. Now abandoned, in the time of the Kings, North men came here with strange goods from the Bay of Forochel.
lotr.waypoint.MAENTHIROST=Maenthirost
lotr.waypoint.MAENTHIROST.info=The ancient northern city of Arthedain. Destroyed before the capture of Fornost, it has since become a ghost of the Northern Kingdom's former glory.
lotr.waypoint.MAR_TARMEARON=Mar Tarmearon
lotr.waypoint.MAR_TARMEARON.info=A fortress city on the road to Mithlond. The ancient center of Númenórean aristocracy in Eriador: observatories, libraries, and wondrous gardens stood here. However, this "pearl" of Arnor was destroyed first by the Great Plague, and then by the armies of Angmar.
lotr.waypoint.FELLBEASTS=Vale of the Fell Beasts 
lotr.waypoint.FELLBEASTS.info=A dark valley behind the walls of Mordor infested with fell beasts and evil creatures.
lotr.waypoint.FENNAS_DRUNIN=Fennas Drunin
lotr.waypoint.FENNAS_DRUNIN.info=Located between two rivers, this ancient fortress city is the largest Dunedin settlement in the North, and the only settlement dominated by stone buildings.
lotr.waypoint.FERTILE_VALLEY=Ajtiaz an-Ahâr 
lotr.waypoint.FERTILE_VALLEY.info=One of the great Southron cities, whose famed markets bustle with traders and goods from all across the lands of Harad and Rhûn.
lotr.waypoint.FIELD_OF_CELEBRANT=Field of Celebrant 
lotr.waypoint.FIELD_OF_CELEBRANT.info=The site of the Gondor-Éothéod victory over the Balchoth, which led to the historic Oath of Eorl and Cirion.
lotr.waypoint.FIRST_FIGHT=Gamil-Barûk
lotr.waypoint.FIRST_FIGHT.info=The first battle in the civil war of the Red Mountains took place here.
lotr.waypoint.AZAN_VARDAR=Azan-Vardar
lotr.waypoint.AZAN_VARDAR.info="Shadow Guard" is an outpost guarding the northern borders of Erebor. The fortification was built by the Dwarves of the Iron Hills after the Battle of the Five Armies to protect the Lonely Mountain from invasions from the north.
lotr.waypoint.FORD_BRUINEN=Ford of Bruinen 
lotr.waypoint.FORD_BRUINEN.info=The shallow ford crossing the Loudwater into the realm of Rivendell, protected by the High Elves.
lotr.waypoint.FORDS_OF_ISEN=Fords of Isen
lotr.waypoint.FORDS_OF_ISEN.info=Gates in land of Rohan, torn by the war between orcs and humans
lotr.waypoint.FOREST_GATE=Forest gate
lotr.waypoint.FOREST_GATE.info=Previously, they were the entrance to the elven kingdom of Greenwood. Now these gates and the surrounding lands belong to the Enemy.
lotr.waypoint.FOREST_SHELTER=Forest Shelter
lotr.waypoint.FOREST_SHELTER.info="Forest Shelter" is the largest known settlement of the woodmen, where travelers can find food and shelter.
lotr.waypoint.FORLINDON=Forlindon
lotr.waypoint.FORLINDON.info=The northern regions of the fair country of Lindon
lotr.waypoint.FORLOND=Forlond 
lotr.waypoint.FORLOND.info=A harbour-city of the Elves on the northern shore of the Gulf of Lune on the southern part of Forlindon.
lotr.waypoint.FORNOST=Fornost
lotr.waypoint.FORNOST.info=Fornost Erain, the ruined capital of Arnor. Known as Kings' Norbury in the Common Tongue. It was also the capital of Arthedain.
lotr.waypoint.FORSAKEN_INN=Forsaken inn
lotr.waypoint.FORSAKEN_INN.info=It is located a day's journey east of Bree, the last human settlement before the wildlands.
lotr.waypoint.FRAMSBURG=Framsburg
lotr.waypoint.FRAMSBURG.info=The ruined city of the Éothéod, Northmen ancestors of the Rohirrim.
lotr.waypoint.FRECA_HOLD=Freca hold
lotr.waypoint.FRECA_HOLD.info=An old fort built by Freсa, who ruled the lands around the Adorn River and was said to be half dunlending.
lotr.waypoint.FROGMORTON=Frogmorton
lotr.waypoint.FROGMORTON.info=A village upon the East Road by the Frog-marshes. It is a marshy village in the Eastfarthing of the Shire.
lotr.waypoint.GALIBUR=Galibur
lotr.waypoint.GALIBUR.info=The old fortress of Galibur. It stands majestically on the hilly highlands of the Ered Tartonion.
lotr.waypoint.GARDENS_BERUTHIEL=Beruthiel gardens
lotr.waypoint.GARDENS_BERUTHIEL.info=Beautiful hanging gardens of Harad. They are said to have been built long ago by a jealous haradian warlord in love with the legendary Queen Beruthiel.
lotr.waypoint.GARGASH=Gargash
lotr.waypoint.GARGASH.info=The abandoned and ruined fortress of the Orcs of Angmar.
lotr.waypoint.GATE_FUINUR=Anat-en-Fuinur
lotr.waypoint.GATE_FUINUR.info=Built long ago by Fuinur's orders, this fortified city protects the kingdom of Umbar from enemies from the North.
lotr.waypoint.GATE_HERUMOR=Anat-en-Herumor
lotr.waypoint.GATE_HERUMOR.info=A great fortress, built, as they say, a long time ago on the orders of Herumor himself, and has been guarding Umbar Bay ever since.
lotr.waypoint.GLADDEN_FIELDS=Gladden fields
lotr.waypoint.GLADDEN_FIELDS.info=The watery meeting-place where the Gladden flows down into the Great River Anduin.
lotr.waypoint.GLANIATH=Glaniath
lotr.waypoint.GLANIATH.info=Lebenin port on the Anduin River. Despite the grandeur of Pelargir, Glaniath was renowned for its fishing industry and ship repair yards.
lotr.waypoint.GLENHIR=Glenhir
lotr.waypoint.GLENHIR.info=The city is located at the junction of two great rivers of western Gondor - Ringlo and Morthond. Located near the port of Edellond.
lotr.waypoint.GOBLIN_TOWN=Goblin town
lotr.waypoint.GOBLIN_TOWN.info=A warren of weaving tunnels and caverns beneath the High Pass, where Orcs scutter and scrape in the dark. A large goblin dwelling in the Misty Mountains, ruled by the Great Goblin.
lotr.waypoint.GREAT_PLAINS_EAST=Hill of the Sun 
lotr.waypoint.GREAT_PLAINS_EAST.info=Among the Morwaith, it is told that here a great ancestral chieftain lies resting, who long ago led their people out from the Shadow into the Sunlands.
lotr.waypoint.GREAT_PLAINS_NORTH=Hunters’ Haunt 
lotr.waypoint.GREAT_PLAINS_NORTH.info=The northernmost regions of the Far Harad grasslands, often visited by poachers from Near Harad who capture and kill exotic beats for a profit
lotr.waypoint.GREAT_PLAINS_SOUTH=Deep Harad
lotr.waypoint.GREAT_PLAINS_SOUTH.info=Not far from here are the towering chain of volcanic mountains which the Morwaith fearfully name the Gates of Fire, Narennyn in the Elven-tongue.
lotr.waypoint.GREAT_PLAINS_WEST.info=The Morwaith of the western plains say that beyond the mountains a Great Lion lies watching, awaiting the day when he will swallow all lands and end the world of Men.
lotr.waypoint.GREAT_PLAINS_WEST=Upper Floodplains
lotr.waypoint.GREEN_HILLS.info=The beautiful Green Hills in western Gondor.
lotr.waypoint.GREEN_HILLS=Pinnath Gelin
lotr.waypoint.GREENHOLM=Greenholm
lotr.waypoint.GREENHOLM.info=A small town upon the Far Downs at the western border of the Shire on the Great East Road.
lotr.waypoint.GREEN_VALLEY.info=Despite countless battles between the Far Haradrim tribes, these vales at the edge of the forest remain green and lush.
lotr.waypoint.GREEN_VALLEY=Nan Harnagorath
lotr.waypoint.GREENWAY_CROSSROADS=Greenway crossroads
lotr.waypoint.GREENWAY_CROSSROADS.info=Greenway crossroad
lotr.waypoint.GRIMSLADE=Grimslade
lotr.waypoint.GRIMSLADE.info=The city where Grimbold, the marshal of Riddermark, lived.
lotr.waypoint.GROR_GATES.info=A Dwarven stronghold, founded by Gror, the father of the Iron Hills. It serves as a border post into the lands of Dale.
lotr.waypoint.GROR_GATES=Gror's Gate
lotr.waypoint.GULF_CITY.info=Greatest of the Gulfen cities. It is said that the Southrons of the Gulf sacrifice their old and sick to their lord Mulkhêr, keeping their blood strong.
lotr.waypoint.GULF_CITY=Khôpakadar 
lotr.waypoint.GULF_EAST_BAY.info=Although said to be a fair land, these eastern shores are notorious as a haunt of corsairs and outlaws from all across Harad and Rhûn.
lotr.waypoint.GULF_EAST_BAY=Topaz Bay 
lotr.waypoint.GULF_EAST_PORT=Ephalôn
lotr.waypoint.GULF_EAST_PORT.info=A lesser port town in the far eastern reaches of the Gulfen lands.
lotr.waypoint.GULF_FORD=Bridge of Harlanhir
lotr.waypoint.GULF_FORD.info=The bridge over the great Southern Border-water which separates the Gulf from the lands of Far Harad.
lotr.waypoint.GULF_NORTH_TOWN.info=A rich Gulfen city amid the gushing streams of the northern vales, whose people strive to surpass the glory of their southern neighbour.
lotr.waypoint.GULF_NORTH_TOWN=Yaphurushi
lotr.waypoint.GULF_OF_HARAD=Arminazûl
lotr.waypoint.GULF_OF_HARAD.info=Here stands a mighty tower to keep a watch over the sea-passages below, as into the Gulf flow stories, goods, and armies from all across Harad and Rhûn.
lotr.waypoint.GULF_TRADE_TOWN=Bakrîzad 
lotr.waypoint.GULF_TRADE_TOWN.info=A trader-town, where exotic goods from East and South are bought and sold. Many Southron traders have made their fortunes here.
lotr.waypoint.GUNUD_DUM=Gunud-dûm
lotr.waypoint.GUNUD_DUM.info=Gunud-dûm is the capital of the Ironfists dwarves, built in the image and likeness of Zigil-dûm in the Red Mountains.
lotr.waypoint.HALIFIRIEN=Halifirien 
lotr.waypoint.HALIFIRIEN.info=The Holy Mountain, westernmost of the beacon-hills of Gondor. Elendil was once entombed here, and Cirion and Eorl swore their Oath upon its slopes.
lotr.waypoint.HARAD_HORN=Horn of Harad 
lotr.waypoint.HARAD_HORN.info=The southernmost point of the Haradwaith. Such lands as may lie further south, if any, come not into the lore of the Númenóreans nor the tales of the Southrons.
lotr.waypoint.HARAD_LAKES.info=The great inland lakes of Haradwaith, like seas within the plains, home to many flourishing plants and herds of beasts.
lotr.waypoint.HARAD_LAKES=Nin Haecharad 
lotr.waypoint.HARADUIN_BRIDGE=Bridge of Haraduin 
lotr.waypoint.HARADUIN_BRIDGE.info=Once the site of a mighty bridge built by the old Taurethrim, long since crumbled away. The new bridge is now traversed only by Morwaith traders and beast-chainers.
lotr.waypoint.HARADUIN_MOUTH=Ethir Haraduin 
lotr.waypoint.HARADUIN_MOUTH.info=The mouths of the mighty Haraduin, the longest river in the world.
lotr.waypoint.HARLINDON=Harlindon 
lotr.waypoint.HARLINDON.info=The southern regions of the fair country of Lindon.
lotr.waypoint.HARLOND=Harlond 
lotr.waypoint.HARLOND.info=A harbour-city of the Elves on the southern shore of the Gulf of Lune on the northern part of Harlindon.
lotr.waypoint.HARLOND_GON=Harlond 
lotr.waypoint.HARLOND_GON.info=Harlond is the river port of Minas Tirith, where ships sail down the Great Anduin from the southern regions of Gondor.
lotr.waypoint.HARNEN_BLACK_TOWN.info=A small but fortified town of Harnennor. The Haradrim speak of a time when Lord Sauron sent a rain of ash upon their lands, to deliver them from Gondorian invaders.
lotr.waypoint.HARNEN_BLACK_TOWN=Ugrî-zadîn 
lotr.waypoint.HARNEN_RIVER_TOWN.info=A settlement of the Southrons by the river Harnen. Here stands a gruesome tower decorated with the skulls of fallen Northerlings..
lotr.waypoint.HARNEN_RIVER_TOWN=Ninzadîn
lotr.waypoint.HARNEN_ROAD_TOWN=An-batîna
lotr.waypoint.HARNEN_ROAD_TOWN.info=A Southron town beyond the crossings of the Harnen, built upon the meeting of many roads.
lotr.waypoint.HARNEN_SEA_TOWN=Bêlkadar
lotr.waypoint.HARNEN_SEA_TOWN.info=Where the mighty Harnen river meets the Bay of Belfalas stands the greatest stronghold of the Harnedhrim, a rallying-point against their foes to the North
lotr.waypoint.HAY_GATE=Hay Gate
lotr.waypoint.HAY_GATE.info=The guarded North Gate in the Hedge of Buckland. It's located southeast of the Brandywine Bridge.
lotr.waypoint.HAYSEND=Haysend
lotr.waypoint.HAYSEND.info=A village in the south of Buckland at the end of the Hedge. It's located south of Bucklebury.
lotr.waypoint.HELEGROD=Helegrod
lotr.waypoint.HELEGROD.info=Helegrod was a dwarven stronghold in the Misty Mountains, connected by underground passages to Khazad-dûm until an Ancient Evil awoke there. Many dwarves sought refuge there, but the stronghold was destroyed by a cold dragon, and the refugees perished.
lotr.waypoint.HELMS_CROSSROADS=Helms crossroads
lotr.waypoint.HELMS_CROSSROADS.info=Vale near Helm's Deep
lotr.waypoint.HELMS_DEEP=Helm's Deep 
lotr.waypoint.HELMS_DEEP.info=The greatest Rohirric fortress, the Hornburg, which stands in a wide vale beneath the Thrihyrne. Men say that its Deeping Wall has never to this day been breached.
lotr.waypoint.HENNETH_ANNUN=Henneth Annûn 
lotr.waypoint.HENNETH_ANNUN.info=The Forbidden Pool of Ithilien, where the Window-curtain waterfall masks a secret refuge.
lotr.waypoint.HIGH_PASS=High Pass 
lotr.waypoint.HIGH_PASS.info=A long and perilous mountain pass from Eriador into Wilderland where the Great East Road crosses the Misty Mountains.
lotr.waypoint.HIMLING=Himling
lotr.waypoint.HIMLING.info=The peak of the hill of Himring, mostly drowned following the War of Wrath. The small island is off the coast of northern Lindon. It was once an Elven citadel during the First Age.
lotr.waypoint.HOBBITON=Hobbiton
lotr.waypoint.HOBBITON.info=A town of Hobbits in the centre of the Shire, overlooked by the Hill of Bag End. It is most famous for being the original residence of Bilbo Baggins.
lotr.waypoint.ILANIN=Ilanin
lotr.waypoint.ILANIN.info=The northernmost settlement of Dorwinion. A village that sees off and welcomes Kelduin's merchant ships.
lotr.waypoint.IMLAT_KARNEN=Imlad Karnen
lotr.waypoint.IMLAT_KARNEN.info=A cliff-top city destroyed by the Harnedrim. The ruins of one of the few fortresses of Harondor are a great place to prepare for invasions of the lands of Gondor.
lotr.waypoint.IMLOTH_MELUI=Imloth Melui
lotr.waypoint.IMLOTH_MELUI.info=The sweet Valley of Roses within Lossarnach.
lotr.waypoint.IRENSAGA.info=A mountain in the northern White Mountains. Írensaga, located at the entrance to Harrowdale Valley, is a massive mountain with a sawtooth ridge at its summit.
lotr.waypoint.IRENSAGA=Írensaga
lotr.waypoint.ISENGARD.info=A huge ring-shaped fortress in the valley of the Misty Mountains, where the Orthanc Tower of Saruman stands.
lotr.waypoint.ISENGARD=Isengard
lotr.waypoint.ISLE_MIST.info=An island, said to be shrouded in mist, that lies at the very southern edge of the world.
lotr.waypoint.ISLE_MIST=Tol Hîth
lotr.waypoint.JUNGLE_CITY_CAPITAL.info=The greatest of the old Taurethrim cities that still stands, though its glory is long fallen from the days of the ancient empire.
lotr.waypoint.JUNGLE_CITY_CAPITAL=Nohoch Kâh 
lotr.waypoint.JUNGLE_CITY_CAVES=Aktun Kâh 
lotr.waypoint.JUNGLE_CITY_CAVES.info=A mysterious city said to be built among caves in the very heart of the earth.
lotr.waypoint.JUNGLE_CITY_DEEP.info=Deep in the jungle stands this lost city, mysterious and forgotten even to many Taurethrim. It is spoken of in their tales as a place of great wonder.
lotr.waypoint.JUNGLE_CITY_DEEP=Mûmakâh
lotr.waypoint.JUNGLE_CITY_EAST.info=An eastern fortress of the Taurethrim built long ago to watch over the lands of the Haraduin.
lotr.waypoint.JUNGLE_CITY_EAST=Lakin Pâh 
lotr.waypoint.JUNGLE_CITY_NORTH.info=A northern outpost of the Taurethrim, fortified against raids from the plains-dwellers..
lotr.waypoint.JUNGLE_CITY_NORTH=Shaman Pâh 
lotr.waypoint.JUNGLE_CITY_OLD.info=Though now in ruins, the long-lost seat of the first Taurethrim High Kings inspires awe among travellers and natives alike.
lotr.waypoint.JUNGLE_CITY_OLD=Ya'ash Kâh 
lotr.waypoint.JUNGLE_CITY_STONE.info=A great city of carven stone, once a jewel of the Taurethrim empire, but now a mere shadow of its former greatness.
lotr.waypoint.JUNGLE_CITY_STONE=Tûnich Kâh 
lotr.waypoint.JUNGLE_CITY_TRADE.info=Near the western edge of the jungles of Harad stands this ancient trader-town, where the old empire grew mighty out of trade with the Númenóreans.
lotr.waypoint.JUNGLE_CITY_TRADE=Otoch Kâh 
lotr.waypoint.JUNGLE_CITY_WATCH.info=A great citadel built in days long past to keep watch over the warmongering tribes of the south.
lotr.waypoint.JUNGLE_CITY_WATCH=Pishan Kâh 
lotr.waypoint.JUNGLE_LAKES=Emerald Lakes 
lotr.waypoint.JUNGLE_LAKES.info=These lakes within the borders of the forests are a place of great natural beauty.
lotr.waypoint.KALDEBURG.info=Kalderburg, the city of the Stone River, is the capital of the Nenedain people.
lotr.waypoint.KALDEBURG=Kalderburg
lotr.waypoint.KAMET_BRIN.info=Arnor city. After its collapse, it became the capital of Rhudaur. After the defeat of Angmar, he was the first to fall under the attack of the armies of the elves and Dunedain.
lotr.waypoint.KAMET_BRIN=Kamet Brin
lotr.waypoint.KAN_MONH.info="Gate of the Winds" is the capital of the Stormcasts, the most numerous clan of the Rhudaur Hillmen. Here, representatives of the other clans gather to resolve disputes and discuss plans for the invasion on the Edain of Eriador.
lotr.waypoint.KAN_MONH=Kan-Monh
lotr.waypoint.KARGASH.info=Kargash, the great blacksmith city of Khand. It is here that weapons and equipment are created for the entire powerful army of Khand.
lotr.waypoint.KARGASH=Kargash
lotr.waypoint.KELED_GATOL.info=The trading city of the Red Mountains, where other dwarf clans come. According to the legends of the Orocarni clans, it was at this place that Durin the Deathless met their founding fathers.
lotr.waypoint.KELED_GATOL=Keled-Gathol
lotr.waypoint.KHAMUL_TOWER.info=The sorcerous tower of Khamûl, a cruel king of Easterlings in the Second Age.
lotr.waypoint.KHAMUL_TOWER=Khamûl Tower
lotr.waypoint.KHAND_FORD.info=The road to the kingdom of Khand, separated by a river with a Rhûn
lotr.waypoint.KHAND_FORD=Khand ford
lotr.waypoint.KHAND_NORTH_ROAD.info=Here, the Easterling troops are marching south to link up with the Harad and Khand forces.
lotr.waypoint.KHAND_NORTH_ROAD=Khand north road
lotr.waypoint.KRU_HUL.info=One for small Khand settlements across river.
lotr.waypoint.KRU_HUL=Kru-hul
lotr.waypoint.LAKE_HARAD=Chunha 
lotr.waypoint.LAKE_HARAD.info=The Taurethrim speak of these swamplands, said to be their home in ancient days before a great flooding drove their people southwards.
lotr.waypoint.LAR_HUZ.info=The hills at the source of the Redwater. Rich iron mines lie here, giving the river's headwaters a scarlet hue.
lotr.waypoint.LAR_HUZ=Lar-Khuz
lotr.waypoint.LAST_BRIDGE.info=The last bridge on the Great Eastern Road before the Misty Mountains.
lotr.waypoint.LAST_BRIDGE=Last bridge
lotr.waypoint.LINHIR.info=A river town in the south of Gondor, located on the road from Pelargir to Etring.
lotr.waypoint.LINHIR=Linhir
lotr.waypoint.LITASH.info=An orc outpost at the foot of the Misty Mountains. Fortress defended the first approaches to Mount Gundabad. Still in use today.
lotr.waypoint.LITASH=Litash
lotr.waypoint.LITTLE_DELVING.info=A smaller Hobbit town upon the White Downs north of Michel Delving in the far west of the Shire.
lotr.waypoint.LITTLE_DELVING=Little Delving 
lotr.waypoint.LOMOST.info=The "gateway" to the uninhabited regions of Gondor. Here you can sometimes find rare inhabitants of western Gondor who trade wood for fish and metals.
lotr.waypoint.LOMOST=Lomost
lotr.waypoint.LOND_DAER.info=The ancient ruins of Middle-Earth's first Numenor haven
lotr.waypoint.LOND_DAER=Lond Daer
lotr.waypoint.LOND_GALEN.info=Lond Galen was built not so long ago. It was needed after the activation of the corsairs of Umbar, as well as the black numenorians. It has also recently become a small harbor for warships.
lotr.waypoint.LOND_GALEN=Lond Galen
lotr.waypoint.LONGBOTTOM.info=A town in the Southfarthing of the Shire, famous for its Longbottom Leaf. Named for the discovery of pipe-weed.
lotr.waypoint.LONGBOTTOM=Longbottom
lotr.waypoint.LONG_LAKE.info=Upon the Long Lake stands Lake-town, a Northman settlement bustling with trade. Great wealth flows through this town out of Dale and onward to southern lands.
lotr.waypoint.LONG_LAKE=Long Lake
lotr.waypoint.MADBOURNE.info=Madbourne, the city of astronomers. It was here that the first khan of the united Khand, Siddharth the Wise, was born long ago.
lotr.waypoint.MADBOURNE=Madbourne
lotr.waypoint.MAHAL_DUM.info=The ruins of stonefoot city, which used to look like a giant workshop. It was the blacksmiths of this hall who first created the crossbow design, which later spread throughout Middle-earth. It is now destroyed.
lotr.waypoint.MAHAL_DUM=Mahal-Dûm
lotr.waypoint.MAICC_TEMAIR=Maicc-Temair
lotr.waypoint.MAICC_TEMAIR.info=One of the most ancient settlements of the hillmen. Even before the invasion of Rhudaur, the locals were attacked by northern orcs and trolls. After the alliance with Angmar, Maicc-Temair-Temeir became a military camp for the forces of Dark in the Ettenmoors.
lotr.waypoint.MELBURG.info=The ancient trading city of Nenedain, which attracts various merchants from nearby lands
lotr.waypoint.MELBURG=Melburg
lotr.waypoint.MENELTARMA_SUMMIT.info=The summit of the Meneltarma, the Sacred Mountain, which alone survived the downfall of Númenor as an island in the Third Age. The name means "the Pillar of the Heavens".
lotr.waypoint.MENELTARMA_SUMMIT=Meneltarma
lotr.waypoint.MERING_STREAM.info=This stream marks the border between Rohan and Gondor. The Mering springs from a deep cleft in the White Mountains called Dol Firien and flows through the Firien Forest. Trees grow densely along the stream's banks.
lotr.waypoint.MERING_STREAM=Mering stream
lotr.waypoint.METHRAST.info=Metrast Beacon was founded after Gondor lost control of Umbar. Beacon has a relatively large garrison of troops in order to repel the landing of pirates from the sea. It also has a good view of the western part of the strait, in front of the mouth of the Anduin.
lotr.waypoint.METHRAST=Methrast
lotr.waypoint.METIR.info=A small settlement in northern Harondor. Ethir fishermen live here, who transport fish by small ships to Pelargir and other Gondor along the Anduin.
lotr.waypoint.METIR=Methir
lotr.waypoint.MICHEL_DELVING.info=The chief town of the Shire, located in the White Downs, and home to the Mayor of Michel Delving. It is the largest town in all the Shire.
lotr.waypoint.MICHEL_DELVING=Michel Delving
lotr.waypoint.MINAS_BRETHIL.info=The ancient fortress of the Rhudaur princes of House Meloss. They were driven out by Angmar, and the place was destroyed. However, hundreds of years later, the Dúnedain of Angle restored the fortress's central tower, as it serves as an important watchtower on the Mitheithel River.
lotr.waypoint.MINAS_BRETHIL=Minas Brethil
lotr.waypoint.MINAS_BRETHIL2.info=A city on the Serni River, founded near a beech forest, it was famous for its lush wheat fields, welcoming travelers coming from the south.
lotr.waypoint.MINAS_BRETHIL2=Minas Brethil
lotr.waypoint.MINAS_ELDANARYON.info=A large fortress city of the black numenorians of Angmar. It was founded shortly after the black numenorians came to these lands with Witch-King. After the defeat of Angmar, the city was destroyed, and the legions of black numenorians, as well as other minions of Witch-king, were scattered. The process of rebuilding the fortress began several hundred years ago, due to the loss of vigilance of the rangers of Eriador and their small number.
lotr.waypoint.MINAS_ELDANARYON=Minas Eldanarion
lotr.waypoint.MINAS_GIRITHLIN.info=A ruined tower on the banks of the Brandywine River. During the Great Plague, the local ruler locked himself in here, taking all the grain from his subjects. Enraged peasants broke into the tower and killed all its inhabitants, and the lord himself was fed to the mice. However, this did not save them from the Plague.
lotr.waypoint.MINAS_GIRITHLIN=Minas Girithlin
lotr.waypoint.MINAS_MENOST.info=The strategically important fortress of Harondor, for which fierce battles are fought between the South and the North. If the Harnedrim capture this place, an excellent garrison will be obtained for the gradual capture of Amon Eithel. The rangers are doing their best to prevent this.
lotr.waypoint.MINAS_MENOST=Minas Menost
lotr.waypoint.MINAS_MORGUL.info=Once Minas Ithil, the fair Tower of the Moon; now a dark and sickly place ruled by the Lord of the Nazgûl.
lotr.waypoint.MINAS_MORGUL=Minas Morgul
lotr.waypoint.MINAS_ONGOTH.info=One of the last remaining strongholds of Arthedain in the Hills of Evendim. A special force of Knights of the North is stationed here – the hope of returning the Kings to the heart of Eriador.
lotr.waypoint.MINAS_ONGOTH=Minas Onghot
lotr.waypoint.MINAS_TIRITH.info=The great Tower of Guard, capital city of the kingdom of Gondor, built of seven levels of pure white stone with the white Tower of Ecthelion at its summit.
lotr.waypoint.MINAS_TIRITH=Minas Tirith
lotr.waypoint.MINAS_WINION.info=A fortified settlement in the heart of Dorwinion. They prefer the preparation of red wine, beautiful architecture and bustling markets with a wide variety of goods.
lotr.waypoint.MINAS_WINION=Minas Winion
lotr.waypoint.MINDOLLUIN.info=Mount Mindolluin is the easternmost peak of the White Mountains. On the eastern side of the mountain, a narrow ledge connected it to the Hill of Guard, or Amon Tirith, on which the city of Minas Tirith is located.
lotr.waypoint.MINDOLLUIN=Mindolluin
lotr.waypoint.MINRIMMON.info=The fifth beacon-hill and one of the oldest, established before the founding of Rohan.
lotr.waypoint.MINRIMMON=Min-Rimmon
lotr.waypoint.MIRKWOOD_MOUNTAINS.info=The Emyn-nu-Fuin, a range of dark hills rising out of the fog of Mirkwood, which fence out the worst of the Necromancer's corruption.
lotr.waypoint.MIRKWOOD_MOUNTAINS=Mountains of Mirkwood 
lotr.waypoint.MIRLOND.info=One of the oldest numenorian colonies along the shores of Belphalas, it is now a half-abandoned harbor city. Sometimes Harnedor's warriors and Umbar's ships come here, using the place as a military garrison.
lotr.waypoint.MIRLOND=Mirlond
lotr.waypoint.MISTALONDE.info=Previously, it was an important port city of Cardolan, actively trading with Gondor. That's what killed the city. It was from here that the Sixth Plague spread throughout Cardolan. All the townspeople are dead, and now only the wind is walking among their bones.
lotr.waypoint.MISTALONDE=Mistalonde
lotr.waypoint.MITHLOND_NORTH.info=The northern half of Mithlond, the Grey Havens, where Círdan the Shipwright dwells with his people. A great elven port in Lindon.
lotr.waypoint.MITHLOND_NORTH=North Mithlond
lotr.waypoint.MITHLOND_SOUTH.info=The southern half of Mithlond, the Grey Havens, where Círdan the Shipwright dwells with his people. A great elven port in Lindon.
lotr.waypoint.MITHLOND_SOUTH=South Mithlond
lotr.waypoint.MORANNON=Black Gate
lotr.waypoint.MORANNON.info=The great gates of Mordor, wrought of twisted steel and dark stone. None pass unless the Eye of the Dark Tower wills it.
lotr.waypoint.MORDOR_FORD.info=The waters of this ford are colored gray with ash and ash. This is where the path of the Rhûn warriors begins, heading to Mordor and the lands of the West.
lotr.waypoint.MORDOR_FORD=Mordor ford
lotr.waypoint.MORIGOST.info=An outpost on the spurs of the Ephel Duat.
lotr.waypoint.MORIGOST=Morigost
lotr.waypoint.MORKAI.info=The second largest fortress in Angmar. Training camps and reviews were held here before sending troops. Ruined.
lotr.waypoint.MORKAI=Morkai
lotr.waypoint.MORVA_TARTH.info=The outpost at the entrance to the Ettenmoors. In fact, it was the gateway to the lands of Angmar in the north. He was one of the first to take the blow of the army of elves and humans, after the defeat at Fornost. The blow was not contained, the fortress was destroyed.
lotr.waypoint.MORVA_TARTH=Morva Tarth
lotr.waypoint.MOUNT_CARADHRAS.info=The Redhorn, the tallest of the three peaks above the delvings of Khazad-dûm. The mountain is called Caradhras the Cruel and is said to have a will of its own.
lotr.waypoint.MOUNT_CARADHRAS=Mount Caradhras
lotr.waypoint.MOUNT_CELEBDIL.info=The Silvertine, one of the three peaks above Khazad-dûm. Upon its summit stands the fabled Durin's Tower.
lotr.waypoint.MOUNT_CELEBDIL=Mount Celebdil
lotr.waypoint.MOUNT_DOLMED.info=Said to be the awakening-place of two Fathers of the Dwarves, this mountain was cloven in the War of Wrath and diminished in size.
lotr.waypoint.MOUNT_DOLMED=Mount Dolmed 
lotr.waypoint.MOUNT_DOOM.info=Orodruin, the great Fire-mountain in the heart of Mordor, wherein Sauron forged the One Ring long ago, and the only place where it can be destroyed.
lotr.waypoint.MOUNT_DOOM=Mount Doom 
lotr.waypoint.MOUNT_FANUIDHOL.info=The Cloudyhead, one of three peaks above the realm of Khazad-dûm.
lotr.waypoint.MOUNT_FANUIDHOL=Mount Fanuidhol
lotr.waypoint.MOUNT_GRAM.info=A mountain inhabited by Orcs who often trouble the lands of Eriador in the north west of the Misty Mountains.
lotr.waypoint.MOUNT_GRAM=Mount Gram
lotr.waypoint.MOUNT_GREEN.info=The Greenhorn, a mighty peak of the Mountains of Harad.
lotr.waypoint.MOUNT_GREEN=Mount Laegras 
lotr.waypoint.MOUNT_GUNDABAD.info=The mountain under which Durin the Deathless woke up in Ancient Days. It was a sacred place of the dwarves before it was captured by the orcs.
lotr.waypoint.MOUNT_GUNDABAD=Mount Gundabad
lotr.waypoint.MOUNT_METHEDRAS.info=The Last Peak, southernmost of the Misty Mountains, whence flow the rivers Isen and Entwash.
lotr.waypoint.MOUNT_METHEDRAS=Mount Methedras
lotr.waypoint.MOUNT_RERIR.info=A large mountain in the north of the Ered Luin. On the western slopes of Mount Rerir was the fortress of the Noldor of the First House, led by Caranthir, son of Feanor.
lotr.waypoint.MOUNT_RERIR=Mount Rerir
lotr.waypoint.MOUNT_SAND.info=The Sunhorn, a high peak in the northern chain of the Mountains of Harad, and bestowed with much significance by the Haradrim .
lotr.waypoint.MOUNT_SAND=Mount Athras 
lotr.waypoint.MOUNT_THUNDER.info=The Stormhorn, a mighty peak of the southern Mountains of Harad.
lotr.waypoint.MOUNT_THUNDER=Mount Belegwaeras 
lotr.waypoint.MOUTHS_ISEN.info=Here, the Isen river flows into the Sea after a long course through the sparsely populated Enedwaith.
lotr.waypoint.MOUTHS_ISEN=Mouth of the Isen
lotr.waypoint.NAN_I_NAUGRIM.info=The ruins of one of the greatest dwarf fortresses, called "Dwarf Valley". In the past, there were networks of 14 mines located here, which were the main source of precious stones and metals. The dwarves have lost these riches, which is why the location of the fortress is kept secret, with the hope that the gold hunters will not completely destroy this place. The ruins serve as a monument to the history of Ered Luin.
lotr.waypoint.NAN_I_NAUGRIM=Nan-i-Naugrim
lotr.waypoint.NARDOL.info=The third signal hill of Gondor. Nardole was located on the western edge of the Druadan Forest. The hill was at the end of a ridge stretching from the White Mountains. Nardol was distinguished by a particularly large signal light. Near the hill, near the mountains, there is a quarry.
lotr.waypoint.NARDOL=Nardol
lotr.waypoint.NARGROTH.info="Flaming Halls", an observation tower above the pass in the Gorgoroth plateau.
lotr.waypoint.NARGROTH=Nargroth
lotr.waypoint.NARGUN_KHAZAD.info=Capital city of Blacklocks vwarves, serving Black Lord Sauron.
lotr.waypoint.NARGUN_KHAZAD=Nargûn-Khazad
lotr.waypoint.NEEDLEHOLE.info=A city in the Westfarthing of the Shire.
lotr.waypoint.NEEDLEHOLE=Needlehole
lotr.waypoint.NIMRODEL.info=The former home of the elf Nimrodel, who disappeared after her lover Amroth drowned in the Sundering Seas.
lotr.waypoint.NIMRODEL=Nimrodel
lotr.waypoint.NOBOTTLE.info=A city in the Westfarthing of the Shire.
lotr.waypoint.NOBOTTLE=Nobottle
lotr.waypoint.NOGROD.info=The ancient city of the dwarves of the Blue Mountains, built in Ancient Days. It was destroyed after the War of Wrath, but then rebuilt by the dwarves.
lotr.waypoint.NOGROD=Nogrod
lotr.waypoint.NORTH_DOWNS=Amon Tyrion
lotr.waypoint.NORTH_DOWNS.info=A defensive tower among the hills located in the north of Eriador. It guards the south-western route, where the ancient city of Fornost is located.
lotr.waypoint.NORTH_DUNLAND=Dunard
lotr.waypoint.NORTH_DUNLAND.info=A fortress in the northern forests of Dunland.
lotr.waypoint.NORTH_ITHILIEN=Cormalle
lotr.waypoint.NORTH_ITHILIEN.info=The northern part of the "Lands of the Moon".
lotr.waypoint.NORTH_UNDEEP.info=The northern of the two western bends in Anduin. Shallow fords of bends were often used by armies to cross the Great River.
lotr.waypoint.NORTH_UNDEEP=North undeep
lotr.waypoint.NOVIG_DUM.info=The largest dwarf settlement that broke away from the trek to the Wind Mountains. Now the city is abandoned, and its inhabitants have died of cold and hunger.
lotr.waypoint.NOVIG_DUM=Novig-Dûm
lotr.waypoint.NURNEN_EASTERN_SHORE.info=The foggy eastern shores of the Nûrnen Sea.
lotr.waypoint.NURNEN_EASTERN_SHORE=Runûrnen
lotr.waypoint.NURNEN_NORTHERN_SHORE=Fornûrnen
lotr.waypoint.NURNEN_NORTHERN_SHORE.info=The dark northern shores of the Nûrnen Sea.
lotr.waypoint.NURNEN_SOUTHERN_SHORE=Harnûrnen
lotr.waypoint.NURNEN_SOUTHERN_SHORE.info=The gloomy southern shores of the Nûrnen Sea.
lotr.waypoint.NURNEN_WESTERN_SHORE=Annûrnen
lotr.waypoint.NURNEN_WESTERN_SHORE.info=The dim western shores of the Nûrnen Sea.
lotr.waypoint.OATBARTON.info=A village in the Northern part of the Shire.
lotr.waypoint.OATBARTON=Oatbarton
lotr.waypoint.OLD_ELF_WAY.info=Old road, built by Eregion elfs
lotr.waypoint.OLD_ELF_WAY=Old elf way
lotr.waypoint.OLD_FORD.info=The place where the Old Forest Road crosses the Anduin River (the Great River of the Wildlands). There was once a bridge here, but it has long since collapsed.
lotr.waypoint.OLD_FORD=Old ford
lotr.waypoint.OLD_JUNGLE_RUIN.info=Here stand the ruins of an ancient Taurethrim city, overrun by troll-demons in an age long past.
lotr.waypoint.OLD_JUNGLE_RUIN=Kimen Kâh
lotr.waypoint.OLD_RHOVANION.info=Long ago, these lands belonged to the great kingdom of the people of Rhovanion, of which only ruins now remain.
lotr.waypoint.OLD_RHOVANION=Old Rhovanion
lotr.waypoint.OSGILIATH_EAST=East Osgiliath
lotr.waypoint.OSGILIATH_EAST.info=The ruined eastern half of the former capital of Gondor, the site of constant skirmishes between Gondor and orcs of Mordor.
lotr.waypoint.OSGILIATH_WEST.info=The ruined western half of the former capital of Gondor. Gondorian garrisons are stationed in this part of Osgiliath to protect the shores of Anduin from invasions from the east.
lotr.waypoint.OSGILIATH_WEST=West Osgiliath
lotr.waypoint.OST_ANGLEBED.info="Iron-finger Fortress" is a settlement located in the center of Lebenin, at the crossroads of the Southern and Lebenin Roads. The town is located at the foot of the beacon hill of Amon Anglebed, whose light is visible from all four sides of the road.
lotr.waypoint.OST_ANGLEBED=Ost Anglebed
lotr.waypoint.OST_IN_EDHIL.info=Ruined city of Eregion.
lotr.waypoint.OST_IN_EDHIL=Ost-in-Edhil
lotr.waypoint.OSTRON.info=A trading city of Wagon People. Blacklocks dwarves, easterlings and people of the South meet here to exchange goods.
lotr.waypoint.OSTRON=Ostron
lotr.waypoint.OVERHILL.info=A small village north of Hobbiton and the Hill.
lotr.waypoint.OVERHILL=Overhill
lotr.waypoint.PELARGIR.info=The great king's landing, the secure stronghold of Gondor in the south. Previously, it was a major shopping center of the kingdom.
lotr.waypoint.PELARGIR=Pelargir
lotr.waypoint.RAS_MORTHIL.info=The last peak in the west of the White Mountains. The people of Anfalas believe that the wild púkel-men are still here in these lands.
lotr.waypoint.RAS_MORTHIL=Ras Morthil
lotr.waypoint.RAUROS.info=The shores of the Parth Galen lawn at the great waterfalls of Rauros.
lotr.waypoint.RAUROS=Rauros
lotr.waypoint.RAVENHILL.info=A remote hill at the foot of Erebor. The Dwarves built a guard post on the hill, and friendly, intelligent ravens like Cark lived above its peace for many years. It was the ravens who gave the hill its name.
lotr.waypoint.RAVENHILL=Ravenhill
lotr.waypoint.REDWATER_FORD=Firstad
lotr.waypoint.REDWATER_FORD.info=A fortress on the banks of the Redwater River near the eastern border of the Kingdom of Dale, guarding the East-West highway laid by the dwarves.
lotr.waypoint.RENDULL.info=A small town in the Morthond valley.
lotr.waypoint.RENDULL=Rendull
lotr.waypoint.RHOSGOBEL.info=The house of Radagast the Brown, where a great many birds and animals live. Apart from the Woodland Realm, Rhosgobel is the safest place in Mirkwood.
lotr.waypoint.RHOSGOBEL=Rhosgobel
lotr.waypoint.RHUN_CAPITAL.info=The great city of the state of Rhûn, the palace and fortress of the King of the East. Its tall towers are hidden in the clouds, and its gates are cast from pure gold!
lotr.waypoint.RHUN_CAPITAL=Rhûnost
lotr.waypoint.RHUN_EAST_CITY.info=The eastern city of Rhúdel. The locals trade with Harad merchants who visit them.
lotr.waypoint.RHUN_EAST_CITY=Karslan
lotr.waypoint.RHUN_EAST_TOWN.info=A small fortified town on the road to Karslan.
lotr.waypoint.RHUN_EAST_TOWN=Karanoda
lotr.waypoint.RHUN_NORTH_CITY=Atalak
lotr.waypoint.RHUN_NORTH_CITY.info=It is said that the bustling markets and winding streets of this easterling port city frighten all travelers who come here.
lotr.waypoint.RHUN_NORTHEAST.info=Northern borders of Rhúdel. Deep swamps, tall reeds, and the air smelling of rotting plants.
lotr.waypoint.RHUN_NORTHEAST=Rhûn northeast
lotr.waypoint.RHUN_NORTH_FORD=Forunen ford
lotr.waypoint.RHUN_NORTH_FORD.info=Ford across the Forunen river, through which the ancient East-West road passes.
lotr.waypoint.RHUN_ROAD_WAY.info=An ancient dwarven road that stretches eastward from the lands of the Rhûn easterlings all the way to the great halls and halls of the Orocarni.
lotr.waypoint.RHUN_ROAD_WAY=Red way
lotr.waypoint.RHUN_SEA_CITY=Belruck
lotr.waypoint.RHUN_SEA_CITY.info=A city located in the heart of Rhúdel. They say that here, on the clearest days, you can see an island in the sea, hiding among the mists.
lotr.waypoint.RHUN_SOUTHEAST.info=The southern border of the easterling country.
lotr.waypoint.RHUN_SOUTHEAST=Rhûn southeast
lotr.waypoint.RHUN_SOUTH_PASS.info=It is said that this mountain pass was once the lair of the great Serpent from the South. Sauron put him to sleep with his charms.
lotr.waypoint.RHUN_SOUTH_PASS=South pass
lotr.waypoint.RIALOND.info=The port city is located at the intersection of the main roads of Dorwinion. Many merchant ships sail from here, carrying the best wine to Dale and the Woodland Realm.
lotr.waypoint.RIALOND=Rialond
lotr.waypoint.RIVENDELL.info=The hidden calley of Imladris, where Lord Elrond lives with his people in the Last Home east of the sea.
lotr.waypoint.RIVENDELL=Rivendell
lotr.waypoint.RIVER_GATE.info=The outpost of the elves of the Woodland Realm at the end of the Forest River
lotr.waypoint.RIVER_GATE=River gate
lotr.waypoint.RONDALPH.info=The capital of Anfalas. Golasgil's domain. One of the few relatively large cities in Anfalas. It is far inferior in beauty and grandeur to the eastern strongholds of Gondor
lotr.waypoint.RONDALPH=Rondalph
lotr.waypoint.ROND_RHANDIR.info=A small village in western Gondor. The main industry is cattle breeding
lotr.waypoint.ROND_RHANDIR=Rond Rhandir
lotr.waypoint.ROTTEN_OAK.info=The oldest of the large oaks of the Mirkwood region. At the moment, the oak has completely rotted, which is why it is considered the tallest rotten tree in the entire forest. Huntsmen and orcs often use it as a reference point for their hikes.
lotr.waypoint.ROTTEN_OAK=Rotten Oak
lotr.waypoint.RUNGARD.info=The small settlement of Harnedor. It is here that the rich mines used by the harnedrim to produce bronze are located.
lotr.waypoint.RUNGARD=Rungard
lotr.waypoint.RUNNING_FORD.info=A town at a shallow ford on a river Running near the road leading to Old Rhovanion.
lotr.waypoint.RUNNING_FORD=Norburg
lotr.waypoint.SANDHILL_TOWN.info=It is said that this southern city, standing on the sand hills, was the site of a great battle many centuries ago.
lotr.waypoint.SANDHILL_TOWN=Lyfa-Tun
lotr.waypoint.SARN_FORD.info=Stone ford on the southern borders of the Shire. Harmless hobbits don't even know that it is carefully guarded by their human protectors.
lotr.waypoint.SARN_FORD=Sarn Ford
lotr.waypoint.SCARHALD.info=Skarháld is a massive city of the Firebeard clan. It consists of five levels surrounding the fortress of Tarrazhar.
lotr.waypoint.SCARHALD=Skarháld
lotr.waypoint.SCARY.info=A small hobbit village near caves and rocky hills.
lotr.waypoint.SCARY=Scary
lotr.waypoint.SCATHA.info=This was once the lair of Scatha, the mighty longworm slain by the Eotheod people.
lotr.waypoint.SCATHA=Scatha lair
lotr.waypoint.SEREGOST.info=A fortress in the mountains of Mordor. Armies of easterlings are passing through here, heading to Barad-dûr at the call of Sauron.
lotr.waypoint.SEREGOST=Seregost
lotr.waypoint.SERELOND.info=A small port town. It is needed to provide the rest of the regions of Gondor with provisions and timber.
lotr.waypoint.SERELOND=Serelond
lotr.waypoint.SHADOW_POINT=Hardorogost 
lotr.waypoint.SHADOW_POINT.info=The city of the Half-trolls, built on a shore of boiling seas and foundering rocks.
lotr.waypoint.shared.info=Available for %s
lotr.waypoint.shared=%s (General)
lotr.waypoint.SHATR_ZIGIL.info=The highest peak of Wind Mountains. The first refuge of Ironfists, who fled from the conflagration of the war from Zigil-Dûm.
lotr.waypoint.SHATR_ZIGIL=Shathr-Zigil
lotr.waypoint.SHEDUN.info=Orc fortress under Mount Gram and the border fortress of Angmar. There were reviews of orcs arriving in Angmar from the Misty Mountains. From here they spread all over Angmar. Now the fortress lies in ruins.
lotr.waypoint.SHEDUN=Shedûn
lotr.waypoint.SOUTH_DESERT_TOWN.info=On the edge of the hostile Harad Desert, there is a surprisingly lively bazaar where nomadic traders and haradrim poachers trade their exotic wares.
lotr.waypoint.SOUTH_DESERT_TOWN=Izem-Ulzuz
lotr.waypoint.SOUTH_DOWNS=Amon Ghart
lotr.waypoint.SOUTH_DOWNS.info=The settlement of Rangers of the North, located in the south of Eriador.
lotr.waypoint.SOUTH_DUNLAND=Fyrwald
lotr.waypoint.SOUTH_DUNLAND.info=A fortress on the forest hills of Dunland.
lotr.waypoint.SOUTH_FOROCHEL.info=One of the few settlements of the Lossoth people is located here in the middle of the white desert.
lotr.waypoint.SOUTH_FOROCHEL=South Forochel
lotr.waypoint.SOUTH_UNDEEP.info=The southern of the two western bends in Anduin. Shallow fords of bends were often used by armies to cross the Great River.
lotr.waypoint.SOUTH_UNDEEP=South undeep
lotr.waypoint.SPATHLIN.info=The fishing town of Spathlin. It is built at the confluence of two rivers, the Ringló, and its main tributary, the Ciril. 
lotr.waypoint.SPATHLIN=Spathlin
lotr.waypoint.STADDLE.info=A hobbit town in the lands of Bree.
lotr.waypoint.STADDLE=Staddle
lotr.waypoint.STARKHORN.info=Starkhorn is a tall and massive mountain in the Harrowdale Range. Its sharp peak was always covered in snow, and clouds often shrouded it.
lotr.waypoint.STARKHORN=Starkhorn
lotr.waypoint.STARKSHAT.info=A former dwarven observation post located south of the High Pass. Now used by goblins to pillage travelers.
lotr.waypoint.STARKSHAT=Starkshat
lotr.waypoint.STOCK.info=A town by Crepe Creek near the Brandywine River. It is famous for its "Golden Perch" tavern, which sells the best beer from the shire.
lotr.waypoint.STOCK=Stock
lotr.waypoint.TANTTAR.info=The coastal town of Anfalasa. Due to the mild marine climate, agriculture is well developed here.
lotr.waypoint.TANTTAR=Tanttar
lotr.waypoint.TAN_ZIGIL.info="Royal Peak" is the peak ending the eastern chain of the Wind Mountains
lotr.waypoint.TAN_ZIGIL=Tan-Zigil
lotr.waypoint.TARLANG.info=People say that a giant fell on this very spot and broke his neck, forming a mountain pass between the Morthond valley and Lamedon.
lotr.waypoint.TARLANG=Tarlang's Neck
lotr.waypoint.TARNOST.info=A city in Gondor, built in ancient times by the elves, who sailed West long ago.
lotr.waypoint.TARNOST=Tarnost
lotr.waypoint.TARWEN.info=A small fortified town used by the Harnedor chieftains as a good strategic position against the Ithilien rangers.
lotr.waypoint.TARWEN=Tarwen
lotr.waypoint.TAURELONDE.info=The great harbor of Numenor, friendly to the Taurethrim Empire in the old days of their power.
lotr.waypoint.TAURELONDE=Taurelonde
lotr.waypoint.TENGRISHA_PEAK.info=The highest peak of the Khand mountains. According to legend, it is at the foot of this peak that the tomb of Siddharth the Wise is located.
lotr.waypoint.TENGRISHA_PEAK=Tengri-sha peak
lotr.waypoint.THARBAD.info=A ford located at the confluence of the Gwathlo and Glanduin rivers, where the ancient Arnor fortress, which was once the capital of Cardolan, is located; abandoned after the Great Plague.
lotr.waypoint.THARBAD=Tharbad
lotr.waypoint.THAURBAND.info=A fortress city on the banks of the Núrnen, a slave trading base. Uruks take prisoners there before sending them to various parts of Mordor and even beyond.
lotr.waypoint.THAURBAND=Thaurband
lotr.waypoint.THE_TROLLSHAWS.info=A valley with wild dense forests and dark caves inhabited by mountain trolls. Ruins of fortresses of Rhudaur are found everywhere.
lotr.waypoint.THE_TROLLSHAWS=Trollshaws
lotr.waypoint.THIKIL_GUNDU.info=Tikil-gundu, the Steel Ridge, was once a rich mine of the Longbeard dwarves. Now overrun by ogres.
lotr.waypoint.THIKIL_GUNDU=Thikil-Gundu
lotr.waypoint.THORIN_HALLS.info=A dwarf settlement in the Blue Mountains, once ruled by Thorin Oakenshield. Thorin gave his people a new home after Smaug sacked Erebor.
lotr.waypoint.THORIN_HALLS=Thorin halls
lotr.waypoint.THRAIN_HALLS.info=A dwarf settlement founded by Thrain II and the exiles of the Lonely Mountain, where many old mines are still in use.
lotr.waypoint.THRAIN_HALLS=Thrain halls
lotr.waypoint.THRANDUIL_HALLS.info=The underground halls of the Elven King Thranduil. They say they resemble the ancient palace of Menegroth.
lotr.waypoint.THRANDUIL_HALLS=Thranduil halls
lotr.waypoint.THRIHYRNE.info=Thrihyrne is a mountain with three peaks and steep slopes resembling jagged horns. It is located at the entrance to the deep gorge of Helm's Deep on the northernmost branch of the White Mountains.
lotr.waypoint.THRIHYRNE=Thrihyrne
lotr.waypoint.THUIN_BOID.info=The fortress is located on a hill, from which the Great Eastern Highway is clearly visible. It was destroyed during the Angmar Wars, but was rebuilt many years later by the Rangers of the North.
lotr.waypoint.THUIN_BOID=Thuin Boid
lotr.waypoint.TIGHFIELD.info=A city famous for its rope makers.
lotr.waypoint.TIGHFIELD=Tighfield
lotr.waypoint.TOLDIL.info=A transit town. Not far from Lebennin. This city has seen off many soldiers, but not all have met...
lotr.waypoint.TOLDIL=Toldil
lotr.waypoint.TOLFALAS_ISLAND.info=A small rocky island in Belfalas Bay.
lotr.waypoint.TOLFALAS_ISLAND=Tolfalas
lotr.waypoint.TOL_FUIN.info=The highlands of Taur-nu-Fuin, "woods under the night shadow", which survived the flooding of Beleriand.
lotr.waypoint.TOL_MORWEN.info=A lonely hill untouched by the disaster of Beleriand, on which lay the grave of Morwen, the mother of Túrin Turambar.
lotr.waypoint.TOL_MORWEN=Tol Morwen
lotr.waypoint.TOWER_HILLS=Emyn Beraid
lotr.waypoint.TOWER_HILLS.info=The tallest of the white towers built for Elendil by Gil-Galad. It is said that it contained one of Arnor's Seeing Stones.
lotr.waypoint.TOWN_BONES=City of Bones
lotr.waypoint.TOWN_BONES.info=A city built among bones, strange and surreal. Gulf people come here to buyûmakil from morwaith.
lotr.waypoint.TREEBEARD_HILL.info=A rocky ledge standing above the trees of the Fangorn Forest, where you can enjoy watching the forest landscapes of this mighty forest.
lotr.waypoint.TREEBEARD_HILL=Treebeard hill
lotr.waypoint.TROLL_ISLAND.info=Troll Island. Many believe that it was here that a race of cruel half-trolls awakened, but no one dares to say for sure.
lotr.waypoint.TROLL_ISLAND=Tol Torog
lotr.waypoint.TUCKBOROUGH.info=The historical city of the Green Hilly Region. The birthplace of the famous and wealthy Tuck family.
lotr.waypoint.TUCKBOROUGH=Tuckborough
lotr.waypoint.TUMLADEN.info=A valley in southern Gondor between the rivers Celos and Sirith. A flourishing land, dotted with villages on green hills. From here, a hidden mountain path led to the lands of Lossarnach.
lotr.waypoint.TUMLADEN=Tumladen
lotr.waypoint.TUMUNBIZAR.info=The northern peak of the Orocarni mountain range. The sacred mountain of the Stiffbeards and Ironfists.
lotr.waypoint.TUMUNBIZAR=Tumunbizar
lotr.waypoint.TWILIGHT_GROVE.info=One of the large villages of the woodmen, that was distorted by the darkness of Dol Guldur. Now only the broken-ones live here, and there is no trace of its former beauty.
lotr.waypoint.TWILIGHT_GROVE=Twillight grove
lotr.waypoint.UDUN.info=A valley desecrated by orcs near the Black Gate. It is named after Udûn, the first fortress of Morgoth, which was also called "Utumno".
lotr.waypoint.UDUN=Udûn
lotr.waypoint.ULDANAVON.info=A small fishing village located by the Uldona River. As in the rest of Dorwinion, vineyards are located here, but the local population still prefers fishing.
lotr.waypoint.ULDANAVON=Uldanavon
lotr.waypoint.UMBAR_CITY.info=The harbor city of the black numenorians and corsairs, the closest of the great kingdoms of Harad, with a long and brutal history of fighting against Gondor.
lotr.waypoint.UMBAR_CITY=Umbar
lotr.waypoint.UMBAR_GATE=Anat-en-Kastamir
lotr.waypoint.UMBAR_GATE.info=A city that guards the only road to Umbar. Named after the king-renegade of Gondor.
lotr.waypoint.URUK_HIGHLANDS.info=These foothill lands once belonged to Rohan, but now they are devastated and burned by the servants of the White Hand.
lotr.waypoint.URUK_HIGHLANDS=Uruk highlands
lotr.waypoint.UTKARSH.info=Utkarsh, a fortress city. A huge fortress built in ancient times. This is where cataphract warriors are trained.
lotr.waypoint.UTKARSH=Utkarsh
lotr.waypoint.UTUMKODOR_NEST.info=Previously, the mighty dragon Utumkodor lived here, who was defeated by the king of the dwarves Snape.
lotr.waypoint.UTUMKODOR_NEST=Utumkodor nest
lotr.waypoint.UZBADBIZAR.info="Valley of the Kings" - along this mountain gorge lie all the kings and rulers of the Hardbeard people, beginning with their forefather Baraz.
lotr.waypoint.UZBADBIZAR=Uzbadbizar
lotr.waypoint.VALLEY_OF_SPIDERS.info=A sinister and gloomy corner of Mordor, inhabited by the spawn of Ungoliant.
lotr.waypoint.VALLEY_OF_SPIDERS=Valley of Spiders
lotr.waypoint.WAYMEET.info=The city is at the intersection of important Shire roads.
lotr.waypoint.WAYMEET=Waymeet
lotr.waypoint.WEATHERTOP.info=The ruined watchtower Amon Sûl. In the old days, it contained one of Arnor's Seeing Stones.
lotr.waypoint.WEATHERTOP=Weathertop
lotr.waypoint.WELLINGHALL.info=One of Treebeard's cottages, located on the foothills of Mount Methedras.
lotr.waypoint.WELLINGHALL=Wellinghall
lotr.waypoint.WEST_GATE.info=The western gates of Khazad-Dûm, now called Moria: the ancient great halls and mines of the dwarves of the Durin's Folk and their Bane.
lotr.waypoint.WEST_GATE=West gate
lotr.waypoint.WEST_PEAK.info=The "Dim Palace" is a large city in the Iron Hills. Before the restoration of Erebor, it was the capital of the Dwarves.
lotr.waypoint.WEST_PEAK=Azanulinbar-Dum
lotr.waypoint.WHITFURROWS.info=A small town by the Eastern Road.
lotr.waypoint.WHITFURROWS=Whitefurrows
lotr.waypoint.WILLOWBOTTOM.info=A small village near forest.
lotr.waypoint.WILLOWBOTTOM=Willowbottom
lotr.waypoint.WITHERED_HEATH.info=A scorched valley in the Grey Mountains, where the last of the fire-breath dragons is said to be hiding.
lotr.waypoint.WITHERED_HEATH=Withered health
lotr.waypoint.WITHYWINDLE_VALLEY.info=An unexplored and dangerous valley where a Withwindle runs through an Old forest.
lotr.waypoint.WITHYWINDLE_VALLEY=Withwindle valley
lotr.waypoint.WOLD.info=A small town in a sparsely populated part of Rohan. Originally, the plains of the Wold were part of the province of Gondor called Calenardon. In the year 2510 of the Third Age, Gondor was attacked from the north by the Balcoth people. The people of Eotheod came to the aid of the Gondorians, and together they defeated the enemy. As a reward, the governor of Gondor, Cirion, gave his new friends the lands of Calenardon.
lotr.waypoint.WOLD=Wold
lotr.waypoint.WULFBURG.info=The fortress of Freka's son, the self-styled "king" Wulf, who captured Meduseld during the reign of Helm Hammerhand.
lotr.waypoint.WULFBURG=Wulfburg
lotr.waypoint.ZIGIL_DUM.info=The abandoned city of the Ironfists, which after the war with the Blacklocks went to the Wind Mountains.
lotr.waypoint.ZIGIL_DUM=Zigil-dûm
lotr.waypoint.ZIGIL_MARRAN.info=The city, according to legend, was founded by the sons of the great Ironfists blacksmith, who created barazim. It is in ruins
lotr.waypoint.ZIGIL_MARRAN=Zigil-Marran
lotr.waypoint.ZIRAK_DUM.info=The ruined city of the Stonefoot Dwarves. This nation was almost destroyed in a devastating civil war. After the victory of the Blacklocks dwarves in the war with the Stonefoots, they went north and into the Wind Mountains, and mixed with the peoples of the Stiffbeards and Ironfists who lived there.
lotr.waypoint.ZIRAK_DUM=Zirak-dûm
lotr.waypoint.ZUDRUGUND.info=These halls were home to the refugees of Erebor after the dragon's sack of the city. Now these chambers are half-abandoned, but wandering dwarves occasionally visit.
lotr.waypoint.ZUDRUGUND=Zudrugund
